a5092391957","name":"Lei Li","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-f2f22e699b2fbc","name":"2024 4th International Symposium on Computer Technology and Information Science (ISCTIS)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/isctis63324.2024.10699182","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/isctis63324.2024.10699182","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/isctis63324.2024.10699182","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/isctis63324.2024.10699182","query":"image manipulation detection localization","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:04:46Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-5cf97cb890f61b70","title":"AUNet: Learning Relations Between Action Units for Face Forgery Detection","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"2023-06-01","abstract":"Face forgery detection becomes increasingly crucial due to the serious security issues caused by face manipulation techniques. Recent studies in deepfake detection have yielded promising results when the training and testing face forgeries are from the same domain. However, the problem remains challenging when one tries to generalize the detector to forgeries created by unseen methods during training. Observing that face manipulation may alter the relation between different facial action units (AU), we propose the Action-Units Relation Learning framework to improve the generality of forgery detection. In specific, it consists of the Action Units Relation Transformer (ART) and the Tampered AU Prediction (TAP). The ART constructs the relation between different AUs with AU-agnostic Branch and AU-specific Branch, which complement each other and work together to exploit forgery clues. In the Tampered AU Prediction, we tamper AU-related regions at the image level and develop challenging pseudo samples at the feature level. The model is then trained to predict the tampered AU regions with the generated location-specific supervision. Experimental results demonstrate that our method can achieve state-of-the-art performance in both the in-dataset and cross-dataset evaluations.","authors":[{"id":"a5082570989","name":"Weiming Bai","orcid":"0000-0002-6168-2987","institution_ids":["i19820366","i4210165038"]},{"id":"a5068621276","name":"Yufan Liu","orcid":"0000-0002-8426-9335","institution_ids":["i19820366","i4210165038"]},{"id":"a5100410132","name":"Zhipeng Zhang","orcid":"0000-0003-0479-332X","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5109346446","name":"Bing Li","orcid":"0000-0002-5888-6735","institution_ids":["i19820366","i4210155469"]},{"id":"a5114549594","name":"Weiming Hu","orcid":"0000-0001-9237-8825","institution_ids":["i19820366","i4210097554","i4210165038"]}],"institution_ids":["i19820366","i4210097554","i4210155469","i4210165038"],"venue":null,"task_tags":["deepfake_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/cvpr52729.2023.02367","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4386072334","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/cvpr52729.2023.02367","citation_count":68,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4386072334","url":"https://openalex.org/W4386072334","query":"face manipulation detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/cvpr52729.2023.02367","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/cvpr52729.2023.02367","query":"image forgery localization @ CVPR","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:41:50Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-330fb00f00190970","title":"Controllable Guide-Space for Generalizable Face Forgery Detection","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-0fdbb7048cc05b","name":"Ying Guo","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-0182fc12b92360","name":"Cheng Zhen","orcid":"","institut